From 1c40f1fb310ca1924344187718cca10aa9e8628e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duck-brain <duck-brain@localhost>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] duck-brain P17: a network's own servo gains, target filter
 and limits (`<net>.runtime.json`)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The P5 walk (walk_hd1910_p5_v1) was trained with the servos at P = 5,
D = 0, its action applied whole (scale 1.0), the target filtered every
20 ms tick and no supply compensation. None of that is in the ONNX
metadata, and all of it differs from the networks before it.

A network may now carry a manifest beside its file,
`<stem>.runtime.json`: servo_p, servo_d, action_scale, target_alpha,
voltage_adapt, clip_lo/clip_hi (action order) and, optionally, the HOME
at full precision (default_joint_pos is rounded to three decimals). It
is read and checked at load; a wrong one fails the load, as a wrong
network does. A network without one runs as before.

While such a network drives:
- target: raw = clip(home + action_scale * a, clip_lo, clip_hi), then
  target = previous + target_alpha * (raw - previous) on all 14 joints
  it drives, the head included; at the start of driving `previous` is
  the goal the servos held (Controller::anchor_to), not the first raw
  target; Pollen's head/leg low-pass and its action voltage scaling
  stand aside (the latter unless voltage_adapt);
- servos (RobotIo::set_servo_runtime, Feetech only): the 14 joints run
  at its P/D — written at torque-on, read back, with the torque-on's
  41 = 0 check unchanged, or at once if torque is already on; P keeps
  following the gain in proportion; the mouth keeps [feetech]'s P/D; the
  driver's 7.4 / V error factor is off unless voltage_adapt. While no
  network drives, the walking network's settings hold, so bring-up's
  torque-on is at them. A P/D that does not read back fails the
  torque-on.
robot.health: feetech.servos[].p / .d as read back.

Checked against the trace the policy came with (500 ticks): our ONNX
run and our action -> target give max |a - a_ref| 5.6e-17 and
max |target - target_ref| 7.0e-8 (cargo test -p robotd -- --ignored
duck_brain_p5).
